DELETE
FROM folders
WHERE id=2;
SELECT id,folder_id
FROM notes
ORDER BY id;
```
Notes 10 and 11 remain, both in folder 1. Optional practice: predict deleting a folder with no notes. If CASCADE is omitted, our separately validated failed DELETE reports FOREIGN KEY constraint failed and preserves all rows. Current learner checks inspect successful state, not expected-error handling. NO ACTION is not interchangeable with RESTRICT for deferred constraints: RESTRICT acts as soon as the key change occurs even if its constraint is deferred; deferred timing is outside this exercise.

