```
Expected diagnostic in the pinned engine: FOREIGN KEY constraint failed. After catching the statement error, run the following separately to inspect preserved data:
```sql
SELECT id
FROM folders
ORDER BY id;
SELECT id,folder_id
FROM notes
ORDER BY id;
```
Both parents and all three original notes remain. This is the ordinary immediate NO ACTION case, not a deferred RESTRICT demonstration. Current learner SELECT grades do not run expected-error assertions; an error in your normal solution is still an error, not a pass.

after:
```sql
PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;
CREATE TABLE demo_folders(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY);
CREATE TABLE demo_notes(
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  folder_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES demo_folders(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
);
INSERT INTO demo_folders VALUES (1), (2);
INSERT INTO demo_notes VALUES (10, 1), (11, 1), (12, 2);
DELETE FROM demo_folders WHERE id = 1;
SELECT id, folder_id FROM demo_notes ORDER BY id;
```
Only note 12, in folder 2, remains. Notes 10 and 11 were linked to the deleted folder.
